Path [text box] - Display
Click the ellipsis button and select the attribute or the method in the dialog Select Object whose value the
Display displays.
Remarks
If you want to show the value of a global variable, you can type in the path to the Variable itself. You can
also type in an expression, such as buffer.NumMU+1.
The Display supports the data types boolean, integer, real, string, object, time, money, length, weight,
speed, date, and dateTime. If the path you type in is invalid, the background of the text box changes to
red.
Note
F2 opens the dialog of the object, whose name you typed into the text box.
SimTalk
Path [SimTalk] - Display
