Type [drop-down list] - Display
Select how the Display displays the data it records.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• Text
Shows the value as text. For floating point values you can type in the number of decimal places. The
Display can show up to 15 decimal places. For the default setting -1 it shows all existing places. Type in
a positive value to show this number of places in the Frame.
Type the text into the text box Comment on the tab Data.
• Bar and Pie
Maps the value in relation to the Minimum and the Maximum of the range that you specify. They
visualize values inside the range by the height of a bar or a filled segment of the pie. An empty bar/pie
corresponds to values below or equal to the lower bound. A full bar/pie represents values above or equal
to the upper bound. To change the height and the width of the bar/pie graphic, hold down the Shift and
die Ctrl keys and drag the border of the graphic with the left mouse button.
Plant Simulation converts the current value to the range, whose bounds you type in and shows it
averaged.
Type in the Maximum Value of the displayed range of values.
Type in the Minimum Value of the displayed range of values.
Type [drop-down list] - Display
Plant Simulation Help 11-4607
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The Display shows the actual Minimum and Maximum values as dotted lines in the Frame window.
This might not be as accurate as you need them to be. The Display shows the current values on the tab
Data in the text boxes Minimum and Maximum.
Note
The Display can only show numerical values as a bar or a piece of a pie. These are easy to understand
but not necessarily suited if accuracy is important.
To reset the values on the tab to 0, click Reset Values on the tab Data.
